<title>USA: Security First splits stock, ups qtly div.</title>
<headline>Security First splits stock, ups qtly div.</headline>
<dateline>MAYFIELD HEIGHTS, Ohio 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Security First Corp said Wednesday that it has declared a three-for-two stock split, and will raise its quarterly dividend.</p>
<p>The stock split will be in the form of a 50 percent stock dividend, payable July 31, record July 15.</p>
<p>The dividend will be increased nine percent to $0.12, from $0.11 on pre-split shares, equivalent to $0.08 per share following the stock split.  </p>
<p>The cash dividend will be payable June 30, record June 16.</p>
<p>Security First is the holding company for Security Federal Savings and Loan Association and First Federal Savings Bank of Kent. As of March 31, the company had assets of $635 million.</p>
